1
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting
sun over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and let
it fly until it gets there.

3
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:29,360
To Kashiwa,
like the type who was always jogging around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
they laughed at me for staying
just as full of energy as ever.

5
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,140
Where's the good energy?

6
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,680
Even as a man,
there's only grit and determination.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare,
and a streetscape that never changes.

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
It's gentler somehow.

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are calling,

10
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:48,940
it's already getting dark, isn't it.

11
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:53,860
Are you watching the yakitori stall?

12
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:11,160
Thank you for watching.

13
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:31,620
Delicious.

14
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:33,740
Thanks for the meal, Reiko-san.

15
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:35,380
You're welcome.

16
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:36,411
You lot,

17
00:01:36,461 --> 00:01:39,980
don't skip patrol and sit around
drinking tea like it's a holiday!

18
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:42,740
But it's freezing outside!

19
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:44,320
Just a little break won't hurt.

20
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:46,220
Says the guy who rides
around in a mini patrol car!

21
00:01:46,220 --> 00:01:49,340
It's true, it's gotten really cold lately.

22
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:50,820
It's already winter.

23
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:52,840
Speaking of winter,

24
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:55,040
Yes, speaking of winter,

25
00:01:55,940 --> 00:01:58,300
roasted sweet potatoes!

26
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:00,340
Here it comes, here it comes!

27
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:04,720
Delicious, delicious sweet potatoes!

28
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:06,080
Yes, thank you very much.

29
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,300
Mister, one please.

30
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:09,400
Me too.

31
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:11,440
Coming right up, please wait a moment.

32
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:15,120
It's the roasted sweet potato truck.

33
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:16,700
I was thinking of buying one too.

34
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:20,620
Why do women love roasted
sweet potatoes so much?

35
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:23,420
They're the classic winter sweet, after all.

36
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:26,780
They're rich in fiber,
and they're cheap too.

37
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:30,360
At our bio development plant,

38
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,880
we've ended up with way too many sweet
potatoes and don't know what to do.

39
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:34,480
Maybe I'll donate them to the station.

40
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,380
What?!

41
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,600
Hold on a second!

42
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:40,440
Leave those sweet potatoes to me,
I'll get rid of them!

43
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:45,500
Clash! The Station Front Food Stall War!

44
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:54,500
It's me, Ginpachi.

45
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:57,920
What is it, bro?

46
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:59,600
Who's this guy?

47
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,860
It's just an octopus, though.

48
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:05,600
Don't ask me that.

49
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,020
I'm asking what kind of
cut this is supposed to be.

50
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:09,460
The cut.

51
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:12,840
You see, here at our shop,

52
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:17,300
our selling point is having
Japan's biggest octopus.

53
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:19,280
This is way too small.

54
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,120
Sorry.

55
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:21,860
Do it over.

56
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,760
You'll lose the customers' trust.

57
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:24,120
Yes.

58
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:30,100
Didn't your older brother's old company

59
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:32,700
get sued by customers and go under, right?

60
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:33,460
Yeah.

61
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:35,980
They said it was a fraud-like business.

62
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:38,480
That's when I realized something.

63
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:42,260
Doing business honestly and steadily is the best way,
you know.

64
00:03:42,940 --> 00:03:46,320
Excuse me, two orders of takoyaki, please.

65
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:47,740
Yes, coming right up!

66
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:49,420
Here you go, one moment.

67
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,580
Thank you very much for your business.

68
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:54,500
Please come again.

69
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:59,420
That's why I'm now here with you,
my childhood friend,

70
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:02,180
selling 400-yen packs of takoyaki,
aren't we?

71
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:04,160
That's right.

72
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:06,580
A Ferrari!

73
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:08,680
What, you know what that is?

74
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:12,600
Before I got laid off,
I worked as a car dealer, so I know.

75
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:20,400
Someday I'd love to be the kind of
guy who gets to drive a Ferrari around

76
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:23,340
You can't run a food stall from a Ferrari,
you know.

77
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:26,660
Isshōkimō -

78
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:32,620
What was that?

79
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:35,400
A Ferrari roasted sweet potato vendor?

80
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:38,660
No way.

81
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:43,580
But it really looked like the back half of the Ferrari
was a roasted sweet potato stall.

82
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:49,440
It's a Ferrari.

83
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,880
That car from before came back around.

84
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:54,520
Yummy, yummy, yummy.

85
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:57,000
Nakagawa, you're going too fast! Slow down!

86
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,420
We can't keep driving in first gear.

87
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:02,220
Hurry up, or it'll get away!

88
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:04,080
Here it comes.

89
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,800
It really was a Ferrari, wasn't it.

90
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:10,780
It's turned into a roasted sweet potato inn.

91
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:13,080
Damn it.

92
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:15,760
Bro.

93
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:17,420
Are you all right?

94
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:19,000
What a car.

95
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,380
Driving along and dropping
burning firewood...

96
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:26,920
They're back.

97
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:29,240
I'm going to give them a piece of my mind.

98
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,120
Bro.

99
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:31,560
It's a Ferrari, you know.

100
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:33,800
You have no idea what kind
of rich guy is driving it.

101
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:37,120
Are you scared of rich people?
How can you run a takoyaki stall like that?

102
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:44,060
Hey, what do you think you're doing, driving
around with a fire burning on top of your car?

103
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:45,540
What about it?

104
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:47,140
"What about it," you say?

105
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:50,820
Cop.

106
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:57,720
Well, the Road Traffic Act doesn't have any provision banning driving with a fire burning on the cargo bed,
you know.

107
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:58,600
So there.

108
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:03,000
But running a sweet potato shop out of my car is a bit much,
you know.

109
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:15,580
That's too much, isn't it? Fine, I guess I'll park around here and do business.
What, is doing business not allowed? Well, never mind. Good luck.

110
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:23,680
A cop running a food stall, and in a Ferrari, no less!
I don't get it, but carelessly, without a clue...

111
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:30,640
Come on, come on! The world's first
Ferrari sweet potato stall opens today!

112
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:33,740
Step right up, step right up!

113
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,260
Delicious roasted sweet potatoes!

114
00:06:36,260 --> 00:06:36,840
One, please.

115
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:37,860
Two for me.

116
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:40,280
Yes, yes, thank you very much.

117
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,380
So cool!

118
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:45,100
Hey, you don't get to leave
without buying something!

119
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,440
Would you ladies like another one?

120
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:49,540
Here you go.

121
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:55,360
Look at all those customers.

122
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:58,920
They're stealing all our customers.

123
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,740
And it's our busiest time of the day, too.

124
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:03,380
That's just how business goes sometimes.

125
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:06,200
At times like this,
we just have to be patient.

126
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:09,100
Thank you very much.

127
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,500
Please come again.

128
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,560
Three, please.

129
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,020
Three, got it.

130
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:15,200
Two, please.

131
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:15,880
Thank you very much.

132
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:16,660
Thank you very much.

133
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:21,940
What?

134
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:24,700
The sweet potatoes are all gone already?

135
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:25,840
Yes.

136
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:28,360
There were still tons of them yesterday.

137
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,240
Well, the person in charge

138
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:34,380
apparently arranged to donate them to
children in famine-stricken countries,

139
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:36,520
and they were already flown
out on this morning's plane.

140
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:39,120
Well, that's a wonderful story, isn't it?

141
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:41,620
Ugh, and we were just getting started.

142
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:43,840
Trying to run a business
on sheer gut feeling

143
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:46,400
you'd better give up on
that self-serving idea.

144
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:46,895
Nakagawa,

145
00:07:46,945 --> 00:07:50,580
your company has a number
of research labs, right?

146
00:07:50,580 --> 00:07:53,400
Isn't there anywhere else
with surplus sweet potatoes?

147
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:57,500
Well, the potatoes are a bit... from the
aquaculture team at the marine research lab.

148
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:59,760
I heard they have a
surplus of octopus, though.

149
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:00,880
Octopus?

150
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:05,120
That'd end up as takoyaki instead of roasted sweet potatoes,
you know!

151
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,020
Well, takoyaki's not a bad idea either.

152
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:13,620
They're not here today, are they?

153
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:15,280
the Ferrari sweet potato vendor.

154
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:16,360
Other people's business is their own.

155
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,260
Our business is our own.

156
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,580
We've got

157
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:22,940
the selling point of the
biggest octopus in Japan.

158
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,200
Bro.

159
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:29,860
What is it?

160
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,060
Look at that.

161
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:35,160
Takoyaki with a whole octopus inside?

162
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:38,420
Don't be ridiculous.
If they put a whole octopus in each one,

163
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,160
It'd have to grow into something huge like this,
wouldn't it?

164
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:52,000
How do you even sell that,
how do you even eat it?

165
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:54,220
No way that's possible.

166
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:56,560
I'm going to give him a piece of my mind.

167
00:08:56,680 --> 00:09:18,540


168
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:42,700


169
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:44,760
There's a whole octopus in there,
I'm telling you!

170
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:47,100
Look, here it is.

171
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:52,040
It's small,
but there's a whole one in there.

172
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:54,540
A nice little octopus.

173
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:58,620
Come on, come on,
there really is a whole octopus in there!

174
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,660
Is that what a police
officer should be doing?

175
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:03,240
That's practically fraud.

176
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:07,460
You're going to do a performance?

177
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:11,980
To win in this fiercely competitive area in front of the station,
we have to differentiate ourselves.

178
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:14,760
It'll also lead to revitalizing that area.

179
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:17,720
Are you really going to do this?

180
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:18,420
It's fine.

181
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:20,080
It'll definitely get a laugh.

182
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:23,300
Here you go, thanks for waiting.

183
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:24,920
Thank you, as always.

184
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,060
Please come again.

185
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,640
He's not here today

186
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:29,860
Those police officers.

187
00:10:29,860 --> 00:10:31,280
Don't mind them.

188
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:34,060
We just need to keep
steadily grilling takoyaki.

189
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:37,740
Your silver hair's going to catch fire!

190
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:39,080
It'll get scorched, you know!

191
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,420
Sorry.

192
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:41,820
Takoyaki, you see,

193
00:10:42,700 --> 00:10:44,780
you have to pay the utmost attention.

194
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:57,100
Fire!

195
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:01,140
That's the cop, right?

196
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,320
Raise 'em up!

197
00:11:08,020 --> 00:11:09,120
Raise 'em up!

198
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:12,420
Yeah! Come on, baby!

199
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:14,660
It's a dance of fire!

200
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:20,580
Yeah! Takoyaki!

201
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:26,640
Yeah! Takoyaki!

202
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:33,100
Takoyaki's delicious!

203
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:46,700
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

204
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:47,180
Garyaa?

205
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:49,120
Ignore him, don't pay him any mind.

206
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,160
Over here, over here!

207
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:53,100
Whoa, they're really doing it!

208
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:54,160
Roll the camera!

209
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:54,500
Yes!

210
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:56,620
What's going on here?

211
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,440
while doing a fire dance
for the station folks.

212
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:03,000
We got a special tip-off that there's
a takoyaki vendor making takoyaki.

213
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:05,140
Yeah, this one's going
to make great footage.

214
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:05,860
Let's go!

215
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:06,360
Yes!

216
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:10,280
Sure enough, TV stations really
are quick with information.

217
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:12,960
Stop poking your nose into other people's
business and just cut the octopus.

218
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:13,460
Yes.

219
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:15,760
Buy my takoyaki!

220
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:18,020
Take me with you!

221
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:20,240
You're really doing whatever you want!

222
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:21,700
Five, please!

223
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:22,580
Six, please!

224
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:24,040
Thank you!

225
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,080
Thank you for your continued patronage!

226
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:30,900
It's the TV crew. They finally got here.

227
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:33,460
Alright, Nakagawa. Turn up the heat!

228
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:37,480
Senpai,
turning up the heat any more is dangerous.

229
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:40,660
I called the TV crew.
We have to put on a bigger show.

230
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:41,440
But...

231
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:43,560
Hey! Fire!

232
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:46,560
I'll do it myself!

233
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:53,400
Now I'll show you a special show.

234
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,540
Fire!

235
00:12:58,460 --> 00:12:59,220
Senpai!

236
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:00,360
Amazing!

237
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:02,800
Now that's some serious effort!

238
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:12,360
Curl up into a ball.

239
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:13,260
The round shape looks great.

240
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:34,040
Sizzle sizzle sizzle sizzle sizzle...

241
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:44,120
Takoyaki's gone totally hardcore now!

242
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,900
Alright, it's done!

243
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:00,520
Wow, they look delicious.

244
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,140
Okay, taste test time!

245
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:11,700
Delicious, Ryo-chan.

246
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:13,480
You're as skilled as a pro.

247
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:14,700
Right?

248
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:20,660
But normally, taiyaki have bean paste all
the way to the tip of the tail, don't they?

249
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:22,220
This one doesn't have any.

250
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:23,540
No, no.

251
00:14:23,540 --> 00:14:27,040
The tail part is like an ice cream cone.

252
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:31,260
You eat it crispy after the
sweet stuff to cleanse your palate.

253
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,640
Yeah, it's refreshing and tasty.

254
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:35,800
It really is.

255
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:43,540
Right, this taiyaki set we won in the shopping street raffle came with flour and bean paste too,
so it's pretty authentic.

256
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:51,320
It was, wasn't it? Speaking of bean paste, I can make it myself.
Our bio plant has so many adzuki beans we don't know what to do with them.

257
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:52,200
Yone-san, what?

258
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:56,100
If that's the case, leave it to me.

259
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:00,920
Hey, Ginpachi!

260
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:04,160
What is it, bro?

261
00:15:04,740 --> 00:15:05,880
What is this guy?

262
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:10,160
What do you mean? It's just chives.

263
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,940
That's not what I asked.

264
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:14,360
I'm asking what kind of chopping this is.

265
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,800
Chopping?

266
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:17,840
It's not even cut!

267
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:18,740
Sorry.

268
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:21,020
When you cut chives,

269
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:23,480
make your left hand into a
cat's paw and hold it down.

270
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:25,760
Chop it rhythmically.

271
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:29,000
If you can't do that,
you'll never become a proper chef.

272
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,380
As expected, bro.

273
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:33,020
I've been doing this for 25 years.

274
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:34,580
Bro!

275
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:35,460
What is it?

276
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:36,800
There's a weird car...

277
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:37,600
What?

278
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:41,180
Taiyaki

279
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:43,960
Just when the annoying cops disappeared,

280
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,800
now there's a taiyaki shop?

281
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,220
What should we do, bro?

282
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:48,940
Alright!

283
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:51,120
I'll teach you the chirijo!

284
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:53,220
Awesome, bro!

285
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:54,760
Mister, can I have some takoyaki?

286
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:56,020
Welcome!

287
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:59,680
Here you go. It's heavy, so don't drop it.

288
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:00,700
Coming!

289
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:01,320
Bye-bye!

290
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:02,120
Thank you very much!

291
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:04,780
Hey, big brother.

292
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:07,540
This business puts the customer first,
you know.

293
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,600
Alright, let's go! Don't underestimate us!

294
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,120
Two orders of takoyaki, please.

295
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:13,820
Yes, yes, coming right up!

296
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:16,580
This takoyaki is delicious, isn't it?

297
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:18,780
Right? It's the octopus
that makes the difference.

298
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:19,860
Thanks as always.

299
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:20,580
Thank you very much.

300
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:24,840
Hey, big brother, when are we going?

301
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:26,740
Just wait a second.

302
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:32,000
If I don't cook these now,
the customers will have to wait.

303
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,440
Well, yeah, that's true.

304
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:35,560
Let's thicken it up a little.

305
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:37,160
You're pretty meticulous

306
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:38,560
Alright, let's go.

307
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:39,060
Yes.

308
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:41,000
Give me the Reiko one.

309
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,640
Over here, too.

310
00:16:42,060 --> 00:16:43,480
Coming right up, hang on.

311
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:47,120
There are so many people,
we can't get any closer.

312
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:48,360
It's fine.

313
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:51,240
Go back to the shop and
bring me the oil-pouring pipe.

314
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,480
Oil-pouring pipe?

315
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,560
Yes, big brother.

316
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:56,560
Is that spot alright?

317
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:58,760
Alright, now look closely.

318
00:16:58,760 --> 00:16:59,500
Hup!

319
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:02,320
Dogedora!

320
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,400
Who gave you permission to set up shop here?

321
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:13,520
The officer from the other day.

322
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:16,120
What, it's you again? What do you want?

323
00:17:16,120 --> 00:17:18,880
No, please, keep up the good work.

324
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:23,000
What was that about, those two?

325
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,060
No idea.

326
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:29,000
Oh no, if that guy shows up again...

327
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,200
So we're ignoring him this time too

328
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:35,440
Anyway, that guy is sure to affect us too.

329
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:39,700
Like last time.
That's the kind of guy he is.

330
00:17:41,020 --> 00:17:41,820
So then,

331
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:46,060
me, whose company went bankrupt,
and you, who got laid off.

332
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,205
This family business we started together,

333
00:17:48,255 --> 00:17:50,900
has only just begun to find its footing.

334
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:54,120
We can't let it get crushed here.

335
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:55,640
Big brother,

336
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,020
this means war.

337
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:02,080
Everything I've built
up through my know-how,

338
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:03,660
I'll pour it all in

339
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:05,820
and crush that bastard.

340
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:09,920
Big brother.

341
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:18,680
Alright, let's make some money today!

342
00:18:19,660 --> 00:18:20,520
Senpai!

343
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:21,920
What is it?

344
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:24,040
The takoyaki place across the way

345
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:26,200
has turned into a taiyaki shop!

346
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:27,140
What?

347
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:30,820
Custard cream, get your custard cream!

348
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:34,840
Twenty-five years devoted to taiyaki,
the finest taste!

349
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:35,840
One for me, mister.

350
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:36,500
Me too.

351
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:37,880
Here you go.

352
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:39,260
Thank you very much.

353
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:42,380
Bro, business is booming

354
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:46,420
Mark my words,
with this we'll crush that cop's stall!

355
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:51,260
So it's custard cream filling?

356
00:18:51,260 --> 00:18:52,340
Then how about this?

357
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,200
But it's selling well.

358
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,240
Alright, Jazo, that works!

359
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:01,860
Nakagawa, get us some custard cream.

360
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:02,520
Yes.

361
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:07,680
Thanks for waiting!

362
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:08,820
Thank you very much.

363
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:15,120
Custard cream-filled ones
are now available here too!

364
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:17,600
We're now selling diet taiyaki!

365
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:20,580
With less sugar and half the calories!

366
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:22,640
They're also smaller in size.

367
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:25,020
Half the calories, they say!

368
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:26,920
Small and easy to eat!

369
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:30,720
Excuse me, sir/ma'am!

370
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:33,460
Come on in! Come on in!

371
00:19:33,820 --> 00:19:34,180
Thank you very much!

372
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:37,120
Looks like they've stolen our customers

373
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:38,880
Copying us

374
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:41,140
Same old scene as always!

375
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:42,600
What should we do, bro?

376
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:45,640
We'll fight back by adding more variations!

377
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:47,240
What?

378
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,520
Right now, at our shop,

379
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:54,760
we have chocolate, chestnut cream,

380
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:56,700
strawberry jam, and so on.

381
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:59,580
We offer a wide variety of taiyaki.

382
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:01,860
Please come try some.

383
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,580
Chocolate, too?

384
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:05,000
Sounds interesting.

385
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,140
Customer!

386
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:09,940
So that's how you want to play it.

387
00:20:09,940 --> 00:20:13,200
We can add variations
as many times as we like.

388
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:14,620
No way we're losing!

389
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:21,500
Next, the world's first caviar,
truffle, and foie gras, and more!

390
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:25,520
We're selling over 100
kinds of gourmet taiyaki.

391
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:30,260
These are limited-time offers,
so don't miss out!

392
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:31,860
I learned about it from the caviar one!

393
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:33,020
Caviar, you say?

394
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:40,060
This guy really spends money differently, doesn't he?
What do we do now?

395
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:43,500
We have no money, but we'll use our brains!

396
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,680
I've got an idea!

397
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:07,000
It's the world's first rice taiyaki!

398
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,860
It's packed with fillings too!

399
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:13,280
You came up with a brilliant move

400
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:16,360
It's just a rice ball in the shape of a taiyaki,
isn't it?

401
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:18,160
What do we do, senpai?

402
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:20,800
Senpai, senpai!

403
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:23,560
Okay, okay, don't panic, don't panic.

404
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:25,860
Time for a break, time for a break.

405
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:29,040
We're going to win this round with this.

406
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:32,100
Humanity's first okonomiyaki taiyaki!

407
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,660
Put some sauce on it and eat up.

408
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:37,180
It's just okonomiyaki, you know.

409
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:38,540
Well, then, ours is

410
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:43,680
the universe's first takoyaki taiyaki!

411
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:45,620
Three takoyaki to a pack.

412
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:50,540
In the end, the other side went back
to being a regular takoyaki shop.

413
00:21:50,540 --> 00:21:53,160
Ours is all about experimentation.

414
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,720
Taiyaki tempura,

415
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:58,340
Is it any good?

416
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:01,020
No idea! The customers are the guinea pigs!

417
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:16,740
Nakagawa! Move it to a place with no people!

418
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:17,480
Right!

419
00:22:29,620 --> 00:22:31,600
That was close.

420
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:33,160
We barely made it.

421
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:36,200
Don't let that car come this way.

422
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:45,040
He set up the people.

423
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:47,540
Forward, forward, forward!

424
00:22:47,540 --> 00:22:47,920
Go forward!

425
00:22:55,780 --> 00:22:58,760
At least we didn't hit anyone.

426
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:02,900
Big brother! Are you all right?

427
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:05,420
Yeah, thanks for messing up for us.

428
00:23:05,420 --> 00:23:07,120
What's with the formality?
Don't be so distant.

429
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:09,900
But what's going to happen to us?

430
00:23:09,900 --> 00:23:10,820
Looks like it.

431
00:23:12,860 --> 00:23:14,520
What do we do, senpai?

432
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:16,680
Let's jump into the
river and put out the fire!

433
00:23:17,540 --> 00:23:19,380
It's a pool! Jump in over there!

434
00:23:19,520 --> 00:23:20,060
Understood!

435
00:23:20,820 --> 00:23:22,880
That's not a pool, is it?
Look at that color.

436
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:23,880
Huh?

437
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:27,260
Yes! Now we can put out the fire.

438
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:29,160
Even for you, senpai, this -

439
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:30,760
It's oil.

440
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:40,600
Fiction

441
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:43,160
Food stalls are so old-school now.

442
00:23:43,940 --> 00:23:46,340
Honest, steady work really is the best.

443
00:23:46,340 --> 00:23:46,960
Yeah, it is.

444
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:51,440
Damn those shopping district bastards!

445
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:56,580
Hiring a pro debt-collector army to steal my bonus?
That's cowardly!

446
00:23:56,580 --> 00:24:02,760
Every year, you and I have fought the
bonus battle fair and square, haven't we?

447
00:24:03,440 --> 00:24:07,100
See you at Bonus Battle 8 next time.

448
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:10,620
Kameari has it all over there.

449
00:24:11,780 --> 00:24:13,980
Well, surely Kameari has it too.

450
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:19,120
Everyone, come on over to our town!

451
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:20,660
Thank you.

452
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:23,660
Thank you for watching.

